{"t": 1794112871.9448805, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found, fix ready*\n\nCause: upstream ledger `2026.11` started adding a `currency` field to every row. `reports/export.py` builds the CSV with `csv.DictWriter(fieldnames=[\"id\", \"amount\"])`, so any row containing `currency` raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` and the export endpoint failed (502 at the edge).\n\nEvidence: CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` (eu-west-1), 2026-11-04 19:02:11 \u2014 `ERROR export failed: ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` together with `INFO upstream ledger 2026.11 added currency to every row`. Note the log entry predates the reported outage start, so it is worth confirming the same error appears on requests since yesterday evening.\n\nFix: added `currency` to the DictWriter fieldnames in `reports/export.py` (column order id, amount, currency). Verified locally: rows with currency export correctly, and a row missing currency yields an empty cell instead of crashing.\n\nNext: deploy reports-api to ECS; no config or data change needed. Please confirm 502s stop after the rollout."}, "ok": true}
